peasant: session 5a1f... was not read again, so its stored transcript was kept
  what:     this session-scoped harvest index kept the stored copy of session 5a1f... and did not re-read its source
  why:      the source path recorded for this session no longer holds it:
            /sandbox/data/peasant/peasant-sync/__peasant-untracked__--host--workspace/5a1f0c3e-7b2d-4e8a-9c61-0d4b3e2f1a70/5a1f0c3e-7b2d-4e8a-9c61-0d4b3e2f1a70--metadata.json
            (Claude Code removes old transcripts after its retention period; peasant keeps the stored copy)
  where:    session lookup (ingest scoped locate)
  when:     before the session was diffed; its transcript was not re-read or re-indexed
  impact:   the stored transcript, its index and its links were not recomputed, and `peasant open`
            shows the stored copy. The bookkeeping a full harvest does for a recorded session (its
            origin verdict, its metrics, and stored-copy maintenance) ran for it as in a full
            harvest. Start-up maintenance may also have run.
  fix:      nothing is needed to keep using the stored copy. To record this session again, restore a
            transcript at that path (or re-enable its harness), then run
            `peasant --config '/sandbox/config/peasant/config.yaml' --config-dir '/sandbox/config' --data-dir '/sandbox/data' --state-dir '/sandbox/state' harvest --session 5a1f0c3e-7b2d-4e8a-9c61-0d4b3e2f1a70`
            again
